{title: Amazing Grace}
{artist: John Newton}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
[G]Amazing grace! how [C]sweet the [G]sound,
that saved a wretch like [D]me!
[G]I once was lost, but [C]now am [G]found,
was [Em]blind, but [D]now I [G]see.

Verse 2
'Twas [G]grace that taught my [C]heart to [G]fear,
and grace my fears re[D]lieved;
how [G]precious did that [C]grace ap[G]pear
the [Em]hour I [D]first be[G]lieved.

Verse 3
[G]Through many dangers, [C]toils and [G]snares,
I have already come; 'Tis [D]grace
[G]hath brought me safe [C]thus [G]far,
And [Em]grace will [D]lead me [G]home.

Verse 4
[G]The Lord has [C]promised good [G]to
me, His Word my hope [D]secures;
[G]He will my Shield [C]and [G]Portion
be, [Em]As long [D]as life [G]endures.

Verse 5
[G]Yea, when this [C]flesh and [G]heart
shall fail, And mortal life [D]shall
[G]cease, I shall possess, [C]within the [G]veil,
A [Em]life of [D]joy and [G]peace.
